@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

rectangle "CameraX" as Camera
rectangle "Latest-frame Scheduler" as Scheduler
rectangle "MediaPipe Pose" as Pose
rectangle "Ordered Result Gate" as Ordered
rectangle "Serialized Analysis Lane" as Lane
rectangle "Telemetry Sampler + Chunker" as TelemetryStage
rectangle "Coordinate Normalizer" as Normalize
rectangle "Confidence-aware Signal Processor" as Signal
rectangle "Tracking Quality Gate" as Gate
rectangle "Temporal Reset Coordinator" as Reset
rectangle "Exercise Analyzer" as Analyzer
rectangle "Biomechanics Metrics" as Metrics
rectangle "Rule Engine + Episode Tracker" as Rules
rectangle "Cue Arbitrator" as Cue
rectangle "Rep Finalization Assembler" as RepFinalize
rectangle "Overlay / Offline TTS" as Output
queue "Short-lived Telemetry Buffer\nbounded / best-effort" as TelemetryQ
queue "Priority Persistence Queue\nbounded / reserved capacity" as PriorityQ
rectangle "Serialized Batch Writer\ncommandSequence ordered" as Writer
database "Room / SQLite" as Room

Camera --> Scheduler : frame + monotonic timestamp
Scheduler --> Pose : newest eligible frame only
Pose --> Ordered : pose result + source timestamp
Ordered --> Lane : strictly increasing timestamps only
Ordered --> Ordered : discard late/out-of-order result
Lane --> TelemetryStage : ordered PoseObservation\nno image bytes
TelemetryStage --> TelemetryQ : bounded-rate PoseObservationChunk
Lane --> Normalize : ordered pose result
Normalize --> Signal : canonical coordinates
Signal --> Gate : smoothed MovementFrame
Gate --> Analyzer : valid tracking only
Gate --> Output : setup/tracking guidance
Gate --> TelemetryQ : TrackingEvent on meaningful state changes
Gate --> Reset : significant temporal discontinuity
Reset --> Signal : reset filter / velocity state
Reset --> Analyzer : reset rep temporal state
Reset --> Metrics : reset ROM / tempo / path accumulators
Reset --> Rules : interrupt/reset temporal episodes
Reset --> RepFinalize : invalidate current trace/finalization state

Analyzer --> Metrics : phase + movement features
Metrics --> Rules : metrics + phase + confidence
Rules --> Rules : PENDING / ACTIVE / FINALIZED episodes
Rules --> Cue : active actionable issue state
Cue --> Output : selected actionable cue

Analyzer --> RepFinalize : final rep/partial-rep state
Metrics --> RepFinalize : final RepMetric[]
Rules --> RepFinalize : rep-scoped episode finalizations
RepFinalize --> PriorityQ : atomic RepFinalizationBundle
Rules --> PriorityQ : revisioned set-scoped FormEvent updates
Cue --> PriorityQ : CueDelivery only when delivered
PriorityQ --> Writer : priority commands in sequence order
TelemetryQ --> Writer : best-effort short-lived batches
Writer --> Room : serialized transactions

note bottom of Ordered
Inference completion order is not trusted.
Only strictly newer source timestamps may enter stateful analysis.
end note

note bottom of Lane
Normalizer, signal processing, quality gating, analyzer, metrics and rules
share one serialized temporal lane per active set.
end note

note bottom of Signal
Low-confidence/missing landmarks are not treated as valid filter updates.
Confidence-aware filtering prevents garbage from contaminating temporal state.
end note

note bottom of Reset
Tracking gaps, material camera/view changes, or exercise/setup reconfiguration
reset all stateful temporal consumers together.
end note

note bottom of TelemetryStage
Realtime analysis FPS and persisted observation rate are independent.
Sample by monotonic time and chunk multiple observations into a versioned payload.
end note

note bottom of RepFinalize
RepFinalizationBundle groups Rep + final metrics + optional CompactRepTrace
+ rep-scoped FormEvent finalizations for one atomic Room transaction.
end note

note bottom of PriorityQ
Commands have monotonic commandSequence values.
FormEvent writes carry monotonic eventRevision values.
SetCloseBarrier is reserved/non-droppable and uses a highWatermark.
end note

note bottom of TelemetryQ
Best-effort short-lived telemetry may have sampling gaps under pressure.
Dropping it is preferable to delaying coaching.
end note

@enduml
